                <pb facs="0533" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/958: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T12:00:00-04:40">February 2,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Department’s circular telegram February 1, 7 p.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    informs me that at the instance of the Brazilian Government the Dominican
                    Government on January 30 telegraphed the Peruvian Government supporting
                    Brazilian proposal for the settlement of Leticia controversy as fair and
                    reasonable and urging its acceptance by Peru.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
